to exercise the expired drop branch of cacheevict shift those timestamps e g 1000 → 1000 remote config tl ms 100 or that branch silently loses coverage with a 60s ttl and the crap ratchet may regress on cacheevict if 600ms is intended fix the header comment lines 59 63 and say 600ms — but then the pr description s 60s ttl cache one fetch per run claims and the ticket s one fetch per job run design line are no longer true of this change set which needs a note the rename is mechanical every other test references mod remote config tl ms symbolically only the eviction test hardcodes the 700ms assumption |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

